# Design system (P1 — hottest surface in the repo)

> `do-not-touch.mdc` (`alwaysApply`) is the floor. It wins over this rule on any overlap.

## Read first
- `docs/DS_SINGLE_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` — **conflict resolution hierarchy** + V4 absorption map + agent checklist before creating any new class/token.
- **`docs/PORTFOLIO_LAYOUT_REFERENCE.md`** — **obligatoire** si `portfolio.css`, shell rails, ou calibration surfaces portfolio ; **ne jamais supprimer**.
- `docs/CSS_INDEX.md` — file map + which surface owns which token.
- `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` — cascade, tokens `--ct-*`, surfaces graphite + ambient shell, §9 cockpit preview.

## Must avoid
- Business logic, data loaders, server actions inside any CSS / DS file.
- Raw hex / rgb literals for brand colors → use `--ct-*` tokens.
- `dark:` modifiers — dark mode only at MVP, colors come from CSS vars.
- Reintroducing a `--ds-*` namespace, a 2nd green, or a `tailwind.config.js`.

## Anti-regression hard rules (enforced by `pnpm ds:guard`)

These patterns are **banned** in the guarded files (witness page + shared DS primitives).
Any PR that reintroduces them will fail `node scripts/ds-hardcode-guard.mjs`.

| Pattern | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `#A7FB90` (raw hex anywhere) | `var(--ct-accent)` or `color-mix(in_srgb,var(--ct-accent)_<N>%,transparent)` |
| `border-white/<n>`, `dark:border-white/<n>` | `border-[var(--ct-border)]` or `border-[var(--ct-border-soft)]` |
| `text-[10px]`, `text-[11px]` | `text-[length:var(--ct-text-nano)]` or class `ct-bento-label` |
| `tracking-[0.15em]` | class `ct-bento-label` (carries `--ct-tracking-widest`) |
| `text-zinc-400`, `text-zinc-500` | `text-[var(--ct-text-muted)]` or `text-[var(--ct-text-body)]` |

To extend the guard to a new file: add its relative path to `GUARDED_FILES` in `scripts/ds-hardcode-guard.mjs`.

## Canonical admin table pattern

`/admin/customers` is the **witness page** for the admin table DS. Before creating any new admin
list table, read this page. The canonical pattern is:

```tsx
// 1. Header token — never inline the recipe, use the shared constant or ct-bento-label
const TABLE_HEAD = "bg-transparent ct-bento-label";

// 2. Card wrapper — token border, not border-white/*
<section className="flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-[var(--ct-border)] bg-surface-card shadow-sm">

// 3. Section sub-header — ct-bento-label, not text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
<h2 className="ct-bento-label text-[var(--ct-text-body)]">Section title</h2>

// 4. Table — Catalyst Table/TableHead/TableRow/TableCell (already imported in page.tsx)
<Table bleed dense>
  <TableHead>
    <TableRow>
      <TableHeader className={`${TABLE_HEAD} pl-5`}>Column</TableHeader>
    </TableRow>
  </TableHead>
  <TableBody>…</TableBody>
</Table>
```

Do **not** copy-paste raw `th`/`td` with per-cell inline styles. The Catalyst `Table` components
are the single structural primitive for admin list surfaces. `TABLE_HEAD` lives in the page file
as a module-level constant — do not duplicate it across pages; if you need it in a 2nd page,
extract it to `@/components/admin/admin-table-layout.tsx`.

## Validate before done
- Read-only audits: `/ds-tokens` `/ds-spacing` `/ds-typo` `/ds-shadows` `/coherence`.
- After ANY CSS change: `browser_close` then re-`navigate` (Turbopack serves the cached chunk otherwise).

## STOP and ask before
- Reordering `@layer cockpit, theme, base, components, utilities;` (globals.css line 4) — it keeps the `* { padding:0 }` reset from beating Tailwind utilities.
- Editing one of the 11 tokens in `cockpit-shell/tokens.css` that `cockpit.css` `:root` supersedes — base edit has **no visible effect**; edit the live value in `cockpit.css`.
- Removing `layer()` from `tokens-layer.css` — it pulls shell tokens into the `cockpit` layer.
- Re-splitting brand/success accent or adding a 2nd green (one vert: `--ct-accent` #A7FB90).
- Flat-black dashboard bg — reverted, signed comment in `cockpit.css`; keep the ambient light behind opaque panels.
- Dense list/table panel — `material="flat"` on `Card` (same opaque graphite; anti cage-in-cage).
